{title: 202 - Hail Him the King of Glory}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #202 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 202}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]Tell it to every [Fm]kindred [Ab]and nation, [Db/Ab]Tell [Ab]it far [Eb7/Db]and [Ab]near;
[Gdim]Earth's darkest [Cm]night will fade [Bbm]with the [Eb7/Db]dawning, [Ab/Eb]Jesus will soon appear.
[Eb/Bb]Hail Him the King of [Bbm/Db]glory, [Cm/Eb]Once [Fm/C]the Lamb [Ab]for [Cm]sinners slain;
[Db]Tell, tell [Bbm/Db]the wondrous [Db]story, [Ab]"Jesus comes [Eb7/Db]to [Fm/C]reign."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bbm]Hail Him the [Ab]King of [Gdim]glory,
[Ab]Once the Lamb [Bbm/Db]for [Db]sinners slain;
[Ab]Tell, tell the wondrous [Cm/G]story,
[Ab/Eb]"Jesus comes to reign."
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]Nations again [Fm]in [Ab]strife [Db]and commotion,
[Gdim]Warnings [Bbm]by [Ab/Eb]the way;
[Eb/Bb]Signs in the heavens, [Cm/Eb]unerring omens,
[Db]Herald [Ab/Eb]the glorious [Eb7/Db]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]Children of [Gdim]God [Fm]look [Ab]up [Db]with rejoicing;
[Gdim]Shout [Cm]and [Bbm]sing [Ab/Eb]His praise;
[Eb/Bb]Bless'd are they [Bbm/Db]who, [Cm/Eb]waiting [Ab]and [Cm]watching,
[Db]Look [Bbm/Db]for [Ab/Eb]the dawning [Eb7/Db]rays.
{end_of_verse}
